          "message": "Namespaces PR2b: AQL USE/IN NAMESPACE grammar — #3349 (#3736)\n\n## Summary\n\nFinal slice of AletheiaDB Namespaces (#3349): AQL `USE / IN NAMESPACE`\ngrammar sugar that sets a query's namespace read scope. This slice\n**only parses** the clause and lowers it onto the existing `Query.scope`\nIR field — it reuses the PR2/PR3d executor scope wholesale\n(`execute_query` already validates `query.scope` and applies it via\n`with_namespace_scope`: source-leaf filter + traversal boundary +\nranked-result filter). No new execution machinery.\n\n## Chosen grammar (canonical)\n\nContextual keywords (no lexer change —\n`USE`/`NAMESPACE`/`ALL`/`NAMESPACES` match `Token::Identifier`,\nmirroring the `WINDOW`/`ALIGN` precedent; `IN` is the existing reserved\ntoken). Namespace names carry `:` `/` `.` `-`, none of which lex as\nidentifiers, so a name is a string literal (a bare identifier is also\naccepted for simple names):\n\n```\nnamespace_clause ::= (\"USE\" | \"IN\") \"ALL\" \"NAMESPACES\"\n                   | (\"USE\" | \"IN\") \"NAMESPACE\" ns_name (\",\" ns_name)*\nns_name          ::= string_literal | identifier\n```\n\n- `USE NAMESPACE 'agent:a'` → `NamespaceScope::Single`\n- `USE NAMESPACE 'agent:a', 'shared'` → `NamespaceScope::List` (union)\n- `USE ALL NAMESPACES` → `NamespaceScope::All`\n- `IN` is an accepted synonym for `USE`; a lone `all` name maps to `All`\n(mirrors the MCP `\"all\"` selector).\n\nIt is a **prefix** clause alongside `AS OF`/`BETWEEN` and may appear in\neither order; a duplicate clause is a structured parse error.\n\n## Semantics / errors\n\n- Omitted clause ⇒ `scope: None` — prior AQL behavior **unchanged**\n(namespace-agnostic; `execute_aql` back-compat preserved).\n- Name charset/length/reserved (incl. the reserved `all` selector)\nvalidation is delegated to `Namespace::new`, so a malformed name\nsurfaces as a structured `INVALID_ARGUMENT` — identical to the MCP\n`namespace` param, never a silent unscoped result.\n- Unknown namespace ⇒ `NOT_FOUND` at execution (via `validate_scope`);\nempty union ⇒ `INVALID_ARGUMENT`; malformed/duplicate clause ⇒ parse\nerror.\n\nCypher `USE NAMESPACE` is intentionally **out of scope** for this slice\n(AQL only).\n\n## Tests (red→green)\n\n- **Parser** (11): single / union / all / `IN` synonym / bare-identifier\nname / namespace-before & after-temporal / no-clause / missing-name /\nmissing-keyword / duplicate.\n- **Converter** (6): clause → `Query.scope` Single/List/All,\nbare-`all`→All, no-clause→None, malformed-name→error.\n- **Execute isolation** (8, via `execute_aql`): single isolates, union\nspans exactly the listed namespaces, all sees everything, no-clause\nunchanged, unknown→NOT_FOUND, malformed→parse error.\n\n## Guards\n\n- No WAL format change; no MCP registry change (tool count unchanged at\n63); no GDPR-owned files touched (changes confined to `src/query/*` +\n`src/db/query.rs`). `__aletheia_ns` non-leak holds (no property-view\ncode touched). No-clause default unchanged.\n\nRefs #3349.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01B3mvy2HNA1SWx6DTDcZe7x)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
